--TEST--
A `Core\Csv::rows` cell read from `Core\Request::bodyStream()` is a `tainted string`, so a plain `string` variable does not take it — `rule:core-api/a-member-takes-the-source-the-program-holds`, `rule:security/tainted-qualifier`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// The rows read the request body, so every cell carries the body's taint.
foreach (Core\Csv::rows(Core\Request::bodyStream()) as var $record) {
    tainted string $held = $record["0"];
    string $name = $record["0"];
    echo $held, $name, "\n";
}
--EXPECT--

--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0401]: expected `string`, found `tainted string`
  --> case.nvs:5:20
%A
error: aborting due to 1 error
